1
00:00:05,956 --> 00:00:09,960
Great Detective Conan
Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi"

2
00:00:23,540 --> 00:00:25,609
Where...

3
00:00:26,443 --> 00:00:28,945
...on earth am I?

4
00:00:34,151 --> 00:00:38,755
Ran! Oi, Ran, wake up! Ran!

5
00:00:41,258 --> 00:00:43,226
Shin'ichi?

6
00:00:45,195 --> 00:00:46,663
Dad!

7
00:00:46,763 --> 00:00:48,665
Sir...

8
00:00:48,899 --> 00:00:50,167
Ah!

9
00:00:50,367 --> 00:00:52,602
What happened? Where are we...

10
00:00:57,908 --> 00:01:01,178
Shin'ichi, what's this about?

11
00:01:01,278 --> 00:01:02,646
I haven't got a clue.

12
00:01:02,746 --> 00:01:04,648
I can't remember anything.

13
00:01:04,781 --> 00:01:07,851
And what is this all about?!

14
00:01:07,918 --> 00:01:09,986
I told you, I don't know!

15
00:01:11,188 --> 00:01:11,955
"Out of range"

16
00:01:12,022 --> 00:01:14,925
Ah, my cell phone's out of range...

17
00:01:29,372 --> 00:01:34,177
"Beloved Shin'ichi-sama, I'm your fan."

18
00:01:34,211 --> 00:01:36,346
"I've been following your achievements."

19
00:01:36,613 --> 00:01:39,549
"You're a wonderful detective."

20
00:01:39,716 --> 00:01:43,587
"This white room is a present for you."

21
00:01:44,054 --> 00:01:45,856
"Please enjoy yourself"

22
00:01:48,925 --> 00:01:50,727
What is this...

23
00:01:50,827 --> 00:01:52,729
Dunno.

24
00:01:53,763 --> 00:01:59,269
However, the one thing that is for certain
is that someone is holding us prisoner.

25
00:02:00,103 --> 00:02:01,805
Who?

26
00:02:02,405 --> 00:02:04,407
And for what reason?

27
00:02:04,774 --> 00:02:06,910
What's going to happen to us?

28
00:02:07,110 --> 00:02:08,545
Say something, boy detective!

29
00:02:08,578 --> 00:02:10,547
I told you, I'm thinking!

30
00:02:22,692 --> 00:02:25,128
If I'm certain, this date is...

31
00:02:25,729 --> 00:02:30,000
The one where I solved a murder case before.

32
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:31,935
Could it be...

33
00:02:32,068 --> 00:02:35,906
That famous photographer who took his
wife's sister who was a model as his lover...

34
00:02:36,006 --> 00:02:37,307
Yes.

35
00:02:38,208 --> 00:02:39,976
It was that case...

36
00:02:56,693 --> 00:02:58,562
I don't think this'll work.

37
00:02:58,795 --> 00:03:02,732
I just can't betray my older sister anymore.

38
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:03,967
Momoko...

39
00:03:04,034 --> 00:03:07,370
Tsubochi-san, you're my sister's husband.

40
00:03:08,205 --> 00:03:09,906
It's time to end this.

41
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:12,576
You can take your camera back.

42
00:03:26,456 --> 00:03:30,627
Don't tell me...
you've gotten another man?

43
00:03:31,828 --> 00:03:33,930
Why? That couldn't be so.

44
00:03:35,765 --> 00:03:37,367
It is so.

45
00:03:37,867 --> 00:03:39,836
I told you I didn't, didn't I?

46
00:03:40,003 --> 00:03:41,705
Shape up...

47
00:03:43,440 --> 00:03:44,874
Don't mess with me!

48
00:04:24,648 --> 00:04:25,415
Hello.

49
00:04:25,448 --> 00:04:26,750
Ah, is that you Sensei?

50
00:04:26,783 --> 00:04:29,286
I should be arriving at the
model Aida-san's apartment very soon.

51
00:04:29,986 --> 00:04:31,688
Eh? Why?

52
00:04:32,055 --> 00:04:33,423
What, have you forgotten?

53
00:04:33,456 --> 00:04:35,592
We have a photo shoot session
with her at 4 pm.

54
00:04:37,127 --> 00:04:38,528
That's right...

55
00:04:39,462 --> 00:04:41,665
Ah, that's right.

56
00:05:08,391 --> 00:05:09,626
"Komehana City Court"

57
00:05:09,759 --> 00:05:12,195
"5 minutes later"

58
00:05:19,502 --> 00:05:20,270
Yo.

59
00:05:20,370 --> 00:05:22,272
Hello.

60
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:32,115
Aida-san! Are you in?

61
00:05:36,086 --> 00:05:37,921
Ala? It's open.

62
00:05:38,722 --> 00:05:39,989
What?

63
00:05:42,826 --> 00:05:44,294
Who are you? Stop!

64
00:05:46,396 --> 00:05:48,298
Thank you very much!

65
00:05:49,466 --> 00:05:50,266
"High School Student Detective
Kudoć Shin'ichi"

66
00:05:50,333 --> 00:05:53,603
How many hours have I waited while
you had your nails done? Has the sun set?

67
00:05:53,670 --> 00:05:55,939
It's okay from time to time.

68
00:05:56,005 --> 00:05:58,174
Sonoko went to a lot of trouble to
get me those free tickets, after all.

69
00:05:58,274 --> 00:06:01,478
Point is, why do I have to be the one
who goes with you?

70
00:06:01,544 --> 00:06:02,746
Because!

71
00:06:02,912 --> 00:06:06,850
I can't use my hands to shop for dinner
right after having my nails done, can I!

72
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:09,352
So in the end, I'm just your bag carrier.

73
00:06:09,486 --> 00:06:10,720
"Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran"

74
00:06:10,787 --> 00:06:12,722
If all you're gonna do is look at your nails...

75
00:06:12,989 --> 00:06:14,758
...then you've looked
and we're done here now, right?

76
00:06:14,824 --> 00:06:16,493
Geez!
You don't understand at all.

77
00:06:16,526 --> 00:06:20,430
When seeing your reflection in the mirror,
what's important is how the whole balance looks.

78
00:06:20,497 --> 00:06:23,900
Anyhow, I'm absolutely never
going out with you again.

79
00:06:24,367 --> 00:06:25,735
Whaa!

80
00:06:25,802 --> 00:06:27,270
What was that scream?

81
00:06:33,610 --> 00:06:34,644
Are you okay?

82
00:06:35,779 --> 00:06:37,147
Please hang in there!

83
00:06:37,213 --> 00:06:38,248
Ah, it hurts...

84
00:06:38,281 --> 00:06:39,783
What happened?

85
00:06:39,916 --> 00:06:41,785
A robber...

86
00:06:42,519 --> 00:06:44,187
There was a robber.

87
00:06:44,654 --> 00:06:46,489
More importantly, there's Aida-kun!

88
00:06:53,930 --> 00:06:57,300
Aida-san! Please hang in there!
Aida-san!

89
00:06:57,700 --> 00:06:59,302
How's Aida-kun?

90
00:07:00,437 --> 00:07:02,205
It's too late...

91
00:07:06,743 --> 00:07:07,944
Aida-kun...

92
00:07:09,345 --> 00:07:11,047
What is this?

93
00:07:12,916 --> 00:07:15,685
Wake up, Aida-kun!

94
00:07:15,952 --> 00:07:17,187
Aida-kun!

95
00:07:26,062 --> 00:07:27,497
What happened?

96
00:07:27,564 --> 00:07:29,699
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Sato Miwako"

97
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,501
"MPD Investigation Unit One
Takagi Wataru"

98
00:07:31,868 --> 00:07:35,171
That's why, because of your abundant
experience in love, I need your advice.

99
00:07:35,638 --> 00:07:38,475
How would I check the room of a woman
who was living alone...

100
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:41,044
...to see whether or not
they had a boyfriend?

101
00:07:41,311 --> 00:07:42,645
"Private Detective - Mori Kogoro"
What?

102
00:07:42,812 --> 00:07:47,083
Boy detective, just where are you right now?

103
00:07:47,717 --> 00:07:49,452
Never mind about that.

104
00:07:49,486 --> 00:07:53,790
More importantly, give me some ideas about
whether a man has been living here or not.

105
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:59,662
The standard is if there's a toothbrush
or if the toilet seat is up, that's suspicious.

106
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:04,100
After that, look around for hobbies
a man would be into.

107
00:08:04,167 --> 00:08:06,703
Even if she had just started being under
the influence of a boyfriend...

108
00:08:06,769 --> 00:08:08,104
...there should be plenty of those.

109
00:08:08,204 --> 00:08:11,174
Well, well, that would be my method,

110
00:08:11,274 --> 00:08:14,177
...but I think such cases are rare and sad
when they do happen, aren't they?

111
00:08:14,277 --> 00:08:15,245
Thank you.

112
00:08:15,278 --> 00:08:19,782
If a woman is going out with a man that way,
they have plans about seeing each other, right?

113
00:08:19,883 --> 00:08:24,754
The man would have to be especially careful,
and when it gets serious...

114
00:08:24,888 --> 00:08:29,425
...it's really the man you see
crying in the end, it's really the man.

115
00:08:29,726 --> 00:08:31,294
Hey, you hung up on me!

116
00:08:31,928 --> 00:08:33,296
Ah!

117
00:08:35,231 --> 00:08:36,232
She disappeared.

118
00:08:36,432 --> 00:08:38,668
No, it's best if you don't come.

119
00:08:39,035 --> 00:08:40,670
It'd be too big a shock.

120
00:08:41,404 --> 00:08:43,406
It wouldn't be good for
the child inside you, either.

121
00:08:43,673 --> 00:08:46,509
Anyhow, get in touch with
your mother and father...

122
00:08:46,809 --> 00:08:50,246
I see. You were struck by a man
who suddenly ran away from inside.

123
00:08:50,346 --> 00:08:51,414
Yes.

124
00:08:51,614 --> 00:08:54,117
Right with the shock of being hit,
all I could see was a pure white.

125
00:08:54,217 --> 00:08:55,818
It was incredibly powerful.

126
00:08:56,019 --> 00:08:58,521
Kishi-san, what was the weapon
you were attacked with?

127
00:08:58,688 --> 00:08:59,789
I don't know.

128
00:08:59,856 --> 00:09:02,525
But, I think it was an iron pipe or something.

129
00:09:02,659 --> 00:09:04,294
An iron pipe or something...

130
00:09:04,394 --> 00:09:06,496
The time when you were knocked out...

131
00:09:06,529 --> 00:09:07,964
"Cameraman's Assistant
Kishi Kousuke"

132
00:09:08,031 --> 00:09:09,232
Um...

133
00:09:09,299 --> 00:09:11,234
Ah, I'm late in introducing myself.

134
00:09:11,334 --> 00:09:14,871
I'm Kudoć Shin'ichi.
I'm a student going to Teitan High School.

135
00:09:15,238 --> 00:09:17,974
This is the high school detective,
Kudoć Shin'ichi-kun.

136
00:09:18,007 --> 00:09:19,676
He's helping us out in
our investigation this time around.

137
00:09:19,742 --> 00:09:21,744
Eh?! THAT great detective?

138
00:09:22,011 --> 00:09:23,112
"Professional Cameraman
Tsubochi Yuuhei"

139
00:09:23,179 --> 00:09:25,048
Is it as Kishi-san said?

140
00:09:25,114 --> 00:09:26,215
Um...

141
00:09:26,282 --> 00:09:28,851
I'm Tsubochi.
Aida-kun's brother-in-law.

142
00:09:29,118 --> 00:09:31,054
When you say you're her brother-in-law...

143
00:09:31,421 --> 00:09:33,723
Yes, she was my wife's younger sister.

144
00:09:33,856 --> 00:09:35,358
The sisters were close.

145
00:09:35,558 --> 00:09:39,495
Are these photos of Tsubochi-san
and your wife's wedding?

146
00:09:39,696 --> 00:09:40,830
Yes.

147
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:43,800
Ehh...
These are terrific photos.

148
00:09:43,967 --> 00:09:46,369
I long for wedding photos such as these.

149
00:09:46,502 --> 00:09:47,503
Eh?

150
00:09:47,837 --> 00:09:48,705
Ah...

151
00:09:48,805 --> 00:09:51,307
Really?
I'm not interested in having any.

152
00:09:51,374 --> 00:09:53,977
Eh? Eh? Ah, really? Is that right?

153
00:09:54,077 --> 00:09:55,445
- More importantly, Detective.
- Yes?

154
00:09:55,545 --> 00:09:57,246
Haven't you found the criminal yet?

155
00:09:57,347 --> 00:10:00,183
Not that much time has passed since
he hit us and ran off, has there?

156
00:10:00,249 --> 00:10:02,218
We're performing
an intensive search right now...

157
00:10:02,485 --> 00:10:04,220
Please make sure to arrest him!

158
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:07,023
It was a man of large build
with a scar on his forehead.

159
00:10:07,624 --> 00:10:10,259
He had cropped, black hair.
He was incredibly violent.

160
00:10:10,526 --> 00:10:14,197
Cropped, black hair
and with a scar on his forehead...

161
00:10:14,430 --> 00:10:15,898
Where have I hear that before...

162
00:10:15,965 --> 00:10:20,303
Aren't those the features of Murozaki,
the suspect wanted for those serial robberies?

163
00:10:20,370 --> 00:10:23,039
In that case, there's a wanted poster for
that criminal on the lower floor.

164
00:10:23,172 --> 00:10:25,241
Eh? There was?

165
00:10:25,575 --> 00:10:27,644
- Takagi-kun, go and get it.
- Yes. Understood.

166
00:10:27,744 --> 00:10:29,712
I took a photo of it with my cell phone.

167
00:10:29,812 --> 00:10:30,980
I see.

168
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:34,984
"Wanted Criminal
Murozaki Eiji"

169
00:10:35,018 --> 00:10:36,152
How about it?

170
00:10:36,219 --> 00:10:38,287
It's not something I can be
sure about in just an instant...

171
00:10:38,588 --> 00:10:40,390
Still, I think he did resemble him.

172
00:10:40,490 --> 00:10:42,191
I'll urgently arrange for his arrest!

173
00:10:42,358 --> 00:10:45,762
He's a wanted criminal! Those arrangements
would have been made long ago.

174
00:10:45,928 --> 00:10:48,631
What sort of personality
did your sister-in-law have?

175
00:10:49,766 --> 00:10:52,135
She was cheerful and sociable...

176
00:10:52,368 --> 00:10:54,137
...the type with lots of friends.

177
00:10:55,772 --> 00:10:58,241
She had been living abroad for a long time.

178
00:10:59,542 --> 00:11:02,912
After she returned to Japan,
she was actively working for fashion magazines.

179
00:11:03,346 --> 00:11:06,816
She also helped me
in my job by being my model...

180
00:11:07,950 --> 00:11:11,187
She was a very beautiful
and excellent woman.

181
00:11:12,121 --> 00:11:14,490
Was there anyone
who bore a grudge against her?

182
00:11:15,825 --> 00:11:17,660
No way!

183
00:11:18,461 --> 00:11:19,462
Um...

184
00:11:19,562 --> 00:11:21,197
The criminal was a robber, wasn't it?

185
00:11:21,297 --> 00:11:22,665
Why would you ask something like that?

186
00:11:22,732 --> 00:11:26,602
Truth is, I think it was someone
other than a robber.

187
00:11:26,936 --> 00:11:28,104
Eh?

188
00:11:30,406 --> 00:11:32,241
As Tsubochi-san noticed as well...

189
00:11:32,375 --> 00:11:35,712
...Aida Momoko-san had choke marks
on her neck where she was strangled by hand.

190
00:11:35,878 --> 00:11:37,780
However, you two were struck by...

191
00:11:37,914 --> 00:11:40,349
...an iron pipe of some sort that
the criminal had brought with him.

192
00:11:40,616 --> 00:11:44,620
In that case, Aida-san should have been
attacked with that pipe as well.

193
00:11:44,887 --> 00:11:48,925
Yet why would the criminal
kill someone by strangling them?

194
00:11:49,292 --> 00:11:52,829
It's strange they didn't use
that weapon, isn't it?

195
00:11:55,565 --> 00:11:56,866
How is it?

196
00:11:56,899 --> 00:12:00,369
There's no doubt she was strangled
and it was death by suffocation.

197
00:12:01,971 --> 00:12:05,608
Moreover, her personal items were scattered about
and there were traces of pollen left behind.

198
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:07,477
Pollen?

199
00:12:08,010 --> 00:12:09,879
Ah, from those flowers.

200
00:12:09,946 --> 00:12:11,881
Those are Casablancas.

201
00:12:13,850 --> 00:12:15,451
Do you know what they mean
in flower language?

202
00:12:15,885 --> 00:12:20,423
Isn't it... "dignity"?

203
00:12:20,857 --> 00:12:23,893
That has nothing to do with this case...
does it.

204
00:12:24,026 --> 00:12:26,129
I guess it was a robbery after all, wasn't it?

205
00:12:26,229 --> 00:12:29,632
Since he mentioned a scar on the forehead,
I think it's immediately obvious.

206
00:12:29,799 --> 00:12:32,869
Yeah. Wouldn't it have been Murozaki?

207
00:12:33,136 --> 00:12:35,538
But Detective Takagi, take a closer look.

208
00:12:36,072 --> 00:12:38,141
This is the method done by an amateur.

209
00:12:38,374 --> 00:12:40,910
For a professional robbery crime,
to me this is a little...

210
00:12:41,043 --> 00:12:42,378
Yeah. But, but...

211
00:12:42,411 --> 00:12:44,747
A strange man did pop out
from inside here and ran off.

212
00:12:44,981 --> 00:12:46,516
The both of them witnessed him.

213
00:12:46,616 --> 00:12:48,518
That's true, isn't it?

214
00:12:48,851 --> 00:12:51,854
"Just what is the true character
of this stranger..."

215
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:54,390
"...that both Kishi-san
and Tsubochi-san encountered?"

216
00:12:56,225 --> 00:12:58,060
I'm going back home for now.

217
00:12:58,227 --> 00:13:00,429
I'm worried about my pregnant wife.

218
00:13:02,565 --> 00:13:05,368
She suddenly lost her sister like this.

219
00:13:05,768 --> 00:13:06,803
I wonder how big a shock she's had.

220
00:13:06,836 --> 00:13:08,304
Please wait!

221
00:13:08,471 --> 00:13:09,705
Something else?

222
00:13:09,806 --> 00:13:12,608
Once I've looked in on my wife,
I'll talk to the police again.

223
00:13:12,809 --> 00:13:13,943
Some reason I can't?

224
00:13:14,010 --> 00:13:16,412
Well, it's nothing all that big...

225
00:13:16,479 --> 00:13:18,815
...but there is something
I was a little curious about...

226
00:13:19,215 --> 00:13:23,186
When the two of you arrived here,
the front door was open, wasn't it?

227
00:13:23,252 --> 00:13:24,487
Yes.

228
00:13:25,188 --> 00:13:27,356
Why would it have been unlocked?

229
00:13:27,657 --> 00:13:29,458
Normally if a thief is simply
ransacking a place...

230
00:13:29,559 --> 00:13:33,429
...they'd lock the door out of fear.

231
00:13:33,496 --> 00:13:35,431
We just happened to see him at the
same time he was coming out, didn't we?

232
00:13:35,832 --> 00:13:40,069
At the exact same moment
Tsubochi-san and Kishi-san appeared?

233
00:13:40,436 --> 00:13:43,005
Unfortunately, our timing was bad.

234
00:13:43,806 --> 00:13:46,676
Kudoć-kun, what's been
bothering you since earlier?

235
00:13:46,809 --> 00:13:50,513
Truth is, I've been thinking
the same thing over and over.

236
00:13:51,581 --> 00:13:54,116
"Was this really a robbery?"

237
00:13:54,283 --> 00:13:55,284
Eh?

238
00:13:56,419 --> 00:13:57,386
Eh?

239
00:13:59,856 --> 00:14:03,059
A ransacking like this
is the work of an amateur.

240
00:14:03,492 --> 00:14:07,296
I can't help but think
this case is more like...

241
00:14:07,496 --> 00:14:10,833
...a murder that's been covered up
to look like the act of a thief.

242
00:14:12,635 --> 00:14:13,870
Which is it?

243
00:14:13,936 --> 00:14:16,005
We were both attacked by
the criminal, weren't we?

244
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:19,275
It was that guy who wrecked this place.
There's no mistake about that.

245
00:14:19,442 --> 00:14:22,311
A heavy-built man with a scar
on his forehead. With cropped, black hair.

246
00:14:22,378 --> 00:14:24,614
That's right. I know that.

247
00:14:27,016 --> 00:14:31,187
You may be a famous great detective,
but you're still just a high school student.

248
00:14:32,288 --> 00:14:35,057
I want a proper police investigation.

249
00:14:36,259 --> 00:14:39,428
Detective Takagi, Detective Sato,
I'll be counting on you.

250
00:14:40,630 --> 00:14:42,832
Well then, please excuse me for now.

251
00:14:43,432 --> 00:14:45,067
Just one more thing.

252
00:14:45,134 --> 00:14:46,435
What is it?

253
00:14:47,937 --> 00:14:49,238
What is this?

254
00:14:49,305 --> 00:14:51,674
It's a pretty big thing.

255
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:54,076
That's a strobe lamp.

256
00:14:54,577 --> 00:14:57,747
What would such a large strobe lamp
be doing in a model's home?

257
00:15:00,283 --> 00:15:01,651
This is mine.

258
00:15:01,717 --> 00:15:04,921
She said she wasn't just interested in being
photographed but in how photos are taken, too...

259
00:15:04,954 --> 00:15:06,155
...so I loaned it to her.

260
00:15:06,188 --> 00:15:07,757
Ehh...

261
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:09,759
By the way, this strobe lamp...

262
00:15:10,059 --> 00:15:11,994
...is still a little warm.

263
00:15:14,664 --> 00:15:17,233
I wonder if Aida-san was using it?

264
00:15:18,768 --> 00:15:20,736
She said she wanted to study camera work.

265
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:22,905
So there's the possibility she may have.

266
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:25,541
This is enough, isn't it?

267
00:15:26,075 --> 00:15:27,576
Well then, excuse me.

268
00:15:28,477 --> 00:15:31,113
No, this is strange.

269
00:15:31,247 --> 00:15:32,782
What is it this time?!

270
00:15:33,115 --> 00:15:36,252
There's something not in this apartment
that should be here.

271
00:15:36,352 --> 00:15:38,020
What's that?

272
00:15:40,389 --> 00:15:41,457
A camera.

273
00:15:41,824 --> 00:15:42,992
Huh?

274
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:45,928
Aida-san was interested in taking photos.

275
00:15:46,062 --> 00:15:47,596
She even had a darkroom to process them.

276
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:49,598
This strobe lamp is still warm.

277
00:15:49,799 --> 00:15:53,035
Nevertheless, the essential camera...

278
00:15:54,036 --> 00:15:55,571
...isn't here.

279
00:15:55,771 --> 00:15:57,573
Don't you find that strange?

280
00:15:59,175 --> 00:16:01,143
It may have been
one of the things that was stolen.

281
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:02,745
So long, excuse me.

282
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,955
Ah! What a gorgeous full-length mirror!

283
00:16:12,989 --> 00:16:15,524
I hope I can get such a big one for my home.

284
00:16:15,591 --> 00:16:16,559
What are you doing?

285
00:16:16,659 --> 00:16:18,561
Huh? Ala?

286
00:16:18,961 --> 00:16:20,596
It's turned in a strange direction.

287
00:16:20,663 --> 00:16:23,065
It only reflects half of me.

288
00:16:27,169 --> 00:16:29,205
I see!

289
00:16:29,271 --> 00:16:30,740
That's how it was!

290
00:16:30,806 --> 00:16:32,074
Ran, thank you.

291
00:16:32,174 --> 00:16:33,943
Eh? For what?

292
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:36,445
Have you discovered something, Kudoć-kun?

293
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:38,180
I've seen it.

294
00:16:39,515 --> 00:16:41,817
The one and only truth.

295
00:16:49,625 --> 00:16:54,897
Actually, why would this strobe lamp
still be warm after all this time?

296
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:56,832
And then earlier,

297
00:16:57,066 --> 00:16:59,435
Ran found the answer to that for me.

298
00:16:59,902 --> 00:17:02,138
What would that be, Kudoć-kun?

299
00:17:02,705 --> 00:17:05,074
It's this full-length mirror at the front door.

300
00:17:05,608 --> 00:17:07,476
It only shows half your body.

301
00:17:08,010 --> 00:17:09,845
It's angle has been twisted.

302
00:17:10,312 --> 00:17:12,314
Excuse me a moment.

303
00:17:13,582 --> 00:17:15,818
Hmm?
I'm not sure I get it...

304
00:17:16,085 --> 00:17:21,690
The trick was to show the both of them
that there was a criminal...

305
00:17:21,824 --> 00:17:24,026
...when one didn't exist.

306
00:17:28,030 --> 00:17:31,167
First off, the criminal set up
this large strobe lamp...

307
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:34,103
...in a place where it would be
in a blind spot from the door.

308
00:17:34,737 --> 00:17:36,439
And then...

309
00:17:36,739 --> 00:17:40,242
...he adjusted this full-length mirror...

310
00:17:41,010 --> 00:17:42,445
...to be set at an angle.

311
00:17:42,778 --> 00:17:45,714
The rest was just a game of timing.

312
00:17:49,452 --> 00:17:52,088
The moment Kishi-san opened the door...

313
00:17:52,221 --> 00:17:54,490
...the criminal turned on this switch.

314
00:17:57,193 --> 00:17:58,961
And then what happened?

315
00:18:01,097 --> 00:18:05,334
The intense flash of light directly struck
Kishi-san's eyes, blinding him.

316
00:18:05,868 --> 00:18:07,570
Huh? Hang on a sec.

317
00:18:07,636 --> 00:18:10,473
In that case, wouldn't the criminal
have been in this room after all?

318
00:18:10,539 --> 00:18:13,042
If he hadn't been, he wouldn't have been
able to press this switch, would he?

319
00:18:13,109 --> 00:18:16,545
No, this strobe lamp
can be controlled remotely.

320
00:18:17,713 --> 00:18:20,983
It's part of the technology
any pro cameraman would have.

321
00:18:21,350 --> 00:18:24,887
And this flash belongs to
the cameraman, Tsubochi-san.

322
00:18:25,221 --> 00:18:28,090
When the electronic flash function of his
camera is turned on and the shutter released...

323
00:18:28,290 --> 00:18:32,595
...this strobe lamp catches the infrared signal
from it and causes a flash.

324
00:18:32,895 --> 00:18:34,063
Tsubochi-san...

325
00:18:34,163 --> 00:18:39,401
...could you press the shutter on the digital
SLR camera you have around your neck?

326
00:18:40,202 --> 00:18:43,038
Tsubochi-san, if you would please.

327
00:18:56,552 --> 00:18:59,488
Ah! That's that had incredible power!

328
00:18:59,522 --> 00:19:02,024
At this moment,
I can't tell what's going on.

329
00:19:03,726 --> 00:19:06,662
And then, at the same moment of the flash...

330
00:19:06,829 --> 00:19:10,065
...the criminal took his weapon
and hit Kishi-san over the head with it.

331
00:19:10,766 --> 00:19:12,368
Since there was a difference in heights...

332
00:19:12,535 --> 00:19:16,372
...a breeze would have come from
the effect of the impact.

333
00:19:19,875 --> 00:19:22,745
Kishi-san wouldn't have known
what had hit him.

334
00:19:23,612 --> 00:19:24,947
By the way...

335
00:19:25,181 --> 00:19:28,217
...the weapon was probably a tripod.

336
00:19:28,551 --> 00:19:31,954
A pro cameraman carries one
around with him wherever he goes.

337
00:19:32,087 --> 00:19:34,123
Hold on there, you.
Then are you saying...

338
00:19:34,156 --> 00:19:35,524
Yes.

339
00:19:36,225 --> 00:19:38,761
The criminal who killed Aida Momoko-san...

340
00:19:39,862 --> 00:19:43,032
...was you, Tsubochi-san.

341
00:19:45,834 --> 00:19:48,270
How dare you come up with such crap.

342
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:49,905
And I heard you were a great detective.

343
00:19:50,005 --> 00:19:51,340
Are you denying it?

344
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:53,842
Yeah.
All of your nonsense.

345
00:19:54,009 --> 00:19:55,778
This trick you so proudly announced...

346
00:19:55,811 --> 00:19:58,614
...is just one of many possibilities
you could have pointed out.

347
00:19:59,648 --> 00:20:00,849
But...

348
00:20:01,183 --> 00:20:03,118
...in order to treat someone as a criminal...

349
00:20:03,252 --> 00:20:05,120
...it's essential you have evidence.

350
00:20:05,187 --> 00:20:08,624
Weren't you and Aida-san seeing one another?

351
00:20:09,058 --> 00:20:11,093
Your wife's younger sister.

352
00:20:11,260 --> 00:20:12,795
That would have been an excellent motive.

353
00:20:12,895 --> 00:20:14,096
Don't mess with me!

354
00:20:14,196 --> 00:20:16,332
I'm telling you to show me some evidence.

355
00:20:16,432 --> 00:20:19,235
Besides, there's no way I'd betray my wife!

356
00:20:19,401 --> 00:20:22,238
You're awfully eager to get away
from this crime scene.

357
00:20:22,571 --> 00:20:27,509
Isn't that because you want the chance
to conceal some evidence?

358
00:20:27,676 --> 00:20:29,612
Don't joke around.
That's nothing but speculation.

359
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:31,180
In that case...

360
00:20:31,513 --> 00:20:33,449
...you won't mind if we ask
for your camera bag.

361
00:20:33,716 --> 00:20:36,785
Despite having a camera
hanging off your shoulder...

362
00:20:36,986 --> 00:20:39,221
...why are you clinging to
that bag so tightly?

363
00:20:39,989 --> 00:20:41,624
That's just stupid.

364
00:20:42,258 --> 00:20:48,063
A pro cameraman always carries around
not only his camera but another one as backup.

365
00:20:48,397 --> 00:20:50,199
It's just that simple!

366
00:20:50,466 --> 00:20:52,201
Isn't this a film camera?

367
00:20:52,635 --> 00:20:54,837
What's more, it's also a classic camera.

368
00:20:55,104 --> 00:20:57,139
Since you normally work
using a digital camera...

369
00:20:57,373 --> 00:20:59,241
...why would you have
a film camera as backup?

370
00:20:59,408 --> 00:21:01,243
Something wrong with that?

371
00:21:01,443 --> 00:21:02,811
Tsubochi-san.

372
00:21:02,945 --> 00:21:05,147
I regret this,
but you shouldn't pass along lies.

373
00:21:05,447 --> 00:21:06,782
What?

374
00:21:07,182 --> 00:21:08,984
This is my reasoning.

375
00:21:09,318 --> 00:21:11,120
This camera...

376
00:21:12,788 --> 00:21:15,457
...is the true camera that should be
in Aida-san's apartment.

377
00:21:16,058 --> 00:21:19,094
Anyhow, after you had killed Aida-san...

378
00:21:19,228 --> 00:21:22,298
...you noticed the presence of
this camera and took it with you.

379
00:21:25,567 --> 00:21:30,139
Doesn't this camera contain a photo...

380
00:21:30,372 --> 00:21:32,041
...showing evidence of your crime?

381
00:21:32,141 --> 00:21:33,742
That's stupid.

382
00:21:33,842 --> 00:21:38,580
In that case, you won't mind
if we have this camera investigated.

383
00:21:40,616 --> 00:21:41,917
If...

384
00:21:42,318 --> 00:21:44,553
...something related to a crime
isn't in there at all...

385
00:21:44,820 --> 00:21:46,789
...just what would you do?

386
00:21:47,022 --> 00:21:48,791
At that time...

387
00:21:49,091 --> 00:21:50,959
...I would completely give up
being a detective.

388
00:21:52,361 --> 00:21:54,730
Shin'ichi, are you sure about this?

389
00:21:54,997 --> 00:21:56,398
Yeah.

390
00:21:57,499 --> 00:21:58,767
All right.

391
00:21:59,401 --> 00:22:00,769
Take it.

392
00:22:02,338 --> 00:22:05,040
Well then, the truth.

393
00:22:05,374 --> 00:22:09,812
The photos left in this camera
will give us the answer to that, won't they?

394
00:22:11,947 --> 00:22:13,716
- If you would please.
- Yes.

395
00:22:13,916 --> 00:22:15,217
"It's okay."

396
00:22:15,317 --> 00:22:19,788
"There's nothing in that camera about either me
or Momoko from the time of the crime."

397
00:22:20,055 --> 00:22:23,258
"There's no possibility at all
that anything will come out of it."

398
00:22:32,201 --> 00:22:33,469
Just a little longer.

399
00:22:41,210 --> 00:22:42,811
I can see it.

400
00:23:02,898 --> 00:23:05,701
How about it?
Now you understand, don't you?

401
00:23:06,001 --> 00:23:07,870
I wasn't me who killed her.

402
00:23:07,970 --> 00:23:09,872
It was that thief!

403
00:23:13,242 --> 00:23:16,845
Kudoć-kun! They're identical.
It's the same pollen.

404
00:23:16,979 --> 00:23:18,747
99% probability.

405
00:23:20,048 --> 00:23:21,083
Pollen?

406
00:23:21,183 --> 00:23:22,584
From the camera.

407
00:23:23,352 --> 00:23:28,957
Pollen from the Casablancas at the crime site
were detected on the body of this camera.

408
00:23:31,226 --> 00:23:36,432
By the way, these flowers came to Aida-san
through a local florist this morning.

409
00:23:36,498 --> 00:23:38,700
It was discovered during the investigation
that that's when she bought them.

410
00:23:40,636 --> 00:23:42,805
Why would pollen from these flowers...

411
00:23:42,871 --> 00:23:46,175
...be clinging to your camera when...

412
00:23:46,341 --> 00:23:49,845
...you hadn't even been in
her apartment yet today?

413
00:23:50,913 --> 00:23:52,548
Tsubochi-san...

414
00:23:52,648 --> 00:23:55,417
...right after you murdered Aida-san...

415
00:23:55,751 --> 00:23:57,920
...you touched this camera
with your hands, didn't you?

416
00:24:04,626 --> 00:24:05,794
Lies...

417
00:24:06,562 --> 00:24:09,198
I heard that the pollen was detected...

418
00:24:09,264 --> 00:24:12,334
...throughout the room and on
all the things scattered around.

419
00:24:13,502 --> 00:24:16,872
If you had taken that camera
out of this apartment...

420
00:24:17,172 --> 00:24:20,709
...it's certain pollen would
have been stuck to it, too.

421
00:24:21,176 --> 00:24:22,411
And...

422
00:24:22,478 --> 00:24:24,813
...even if you knew pollen was going around...

423
00:24:25,113 --> 00:24:29,418
...you would still have insisted on always
carrying that camera with you, wouldn't you?

424
00:24:29,618 --> 00:24:31,320
Most likely...

425
00:24:31,386 --> 00:24:35,257
...that camera symbolized
the close relationship you had with Aida-san.

426
00:24:41,163 --> 00:24:42,664
The camera...

427
00:24:43,932 --> 00:24:46,235
Momoko's camera...

428
00:24:46,635 --> 00:24:48,237
To be honest...

429
00:24:48,337 --> 00:24:52,107
...I wasn't really interested in the pictures
contained in that camera.

430
00:24:53,242 --> 00:24:58,647
I just wanted to buy some time to have
the pollen that was stuck to it checked out.

431
00:24:58,947 --> 00:25:01,016
Since you couldn't be arrested
without some physical evidence...

432
00:25:01,183 --> 00:25:05,053
...and since it also clarified
some of your tricks at the same time.

433
00:25:07,556 --> 00:25:08,924
You're wrong.

434
00:25:10,292 --> 00:25:12,160
I didn't do anything bad.

435
00:25:14,329 --> 00:25:15,797
This woman...

436
00:25:16,164 --> 00:25:17,866
This woman was toying with me...

437
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:19,001
That's why I had to do it!

438
00:25:19,034 --> 00:25:20,536
You...

439
00:25:20,903 --> 00:25:23,205
Even so, you're a professional cameraman.

440
00:25:24,306 --> 00:25:26,074
These photos...

441
00:25:26,408 --> 00:25:30,812
Take a good look at the
final photographs that Aida-san took.

442
00:25:44,560 --> 00:25:51,667
I... love... you.

443
00:25:53,702 --> 00:25:55,237
"I love you."

444
00:25:55,504 --> 00:25:57,506
That's what she was saying.

445
00:25:58,473 --> 00:26:01,944
We received a report from
the coroner a moment ago.

446
00:26:02,177 --> 00:26:06,715
They said that after she was strangled,
she lived for quite a while afterwards.

447
00:26:07,516 --> 00:26:08,817
Tsubochi-san.

448
00:26:09,084 --> 00:26:13,455
If you hadn't wasted time trying to cover up your
actions and had called an ambulance immediately...

449
00:26:13,689 --> 00:26:16,792
...she might have been saved.

450
00:26:21,396 --> 00:26:23,599
I'm certain she wanted to protect...

451
00:26:23,999 --> 00:26:28,270
...both her sister and the man that she loved.

452
00:26:30,305 --> 00:26:32,007
Aida-san...

453
00:26:32,174 --> 00:26:35,077
...was trying to suppress the feelings
she had for you...

454
00:26:35,110 --> 00:26:37,045
...and so chose to break up with you.

455
00:26:37,279 --> 00:26:40,582
Such a brave and pure woman...

456
00:26:40,749 --> 00:26:43,318
The woman who loved you
from the bottom of her heart...

457
00:26:43,719 --> 00:26:45,621
With your hand...

458
00:26:45,854 --> 00:26:48,190
...you've buried her in the earth!

459
00:26:52,728 --> 00:26:54,630
Momoko...

460
00:26:58,033 --> 00:27:00,068
I'm so sorry.

461
00:27:01,670 --> 00:27:03,472
Momoko...

462
00:27:07,976 --> 00:27:10,278
Momoko!

463
00:27:17,185 --> 00:27:19,287
I feel so sorry for Aida-san.

464
00:27:19,988 --> 00:27:21,790
Momoko...

465
00:27:35,837 --> 00:27:37,506
Momoko...

466
00:27:38,807 --> 00:27:44,713
"I Love You"

467
00:28:13,575 --> 00:28:17,479
"What is this!
Just who is doing this and why?"

468
00:28:20,082 --> 00:28:23,218
"What're we gonna do?
Hey, Shin'ichi!"

469
00:28:23,285 --> 00:28:25,020
"I told you, I'm thinking about it!"

470
00:28:25,087 --> 00:28:27,756
"YOU DON'T HAVE TO SHOUT!"

471
00:28:49,911 --> 00:29:00,122
"That day...
That was the day of the case where
I confronted that psychic..."

472
00:29:01,089 --> 00:29:03,658
It's said she was killed psychically.

473
00:29:06,027 --> 00:29:08,063
If I recall, that case...

474
00:29:08,163 --> 00:29:09,698
"After this
A New Challenge For Shin'ichi"

475
00:29:10,165 --> 00:29:13,769
"Murdered by Psychic Ability?!"

476
00:29:22,677 --> 00:29:24,146
"This drama is fictional"

